      "file": "slurry_pump_wear.glb",
      "title": "Wear zones",
      "description": "Typical wear pattern of a centrifugal slurry pump. Purple = most severe: throatbush face and impeller front shroud gap (recirculation gouging), impeller eye / vane inlet edges, and the volute cutwater (tongue). Pink = moderate: volute liner around the impeller tip and vane trailing edges. Yellow = light: frame-plate liner / back shroud. Wear grows steeply with particle size, solids concentration and velocity, so slurry pumps run slow and keep the front clearance closed.",
